---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";

export const prerender = true;

const title = "Privacy Policy | Fuel Calculate";
const description =
  "How Fuel Calculate handles cookies, local storage, IP-based country detection, geolocation for the station finder, and third-party services like Google Maps.";
const lastUpdated = "21 July 2026";

const sectionClass = "text-body-md text-body";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Hero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy Policy." lead={`Last updated ${lastUpdated}.`} />

  <section class="mx-auto flex max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-xl px-md pb-5xl sm:px-lg">
    <p class={sectionClass}>
      Fuel Calculate ("we", "us", "this site") does not require an account, does not
      sell personal data, and does not run any advertising or analytics tracking at
      the time of writing. This policy explains exactly what data does flow through
      the site — mostly kept on your own device — and the specific third parties
      involved when you use certain features.
    </p>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Information stored on your device</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        The calculator, comparison tool, and theme preference all use your browser's
        local storage and cookies — never a server-side account:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-sm flex flex-col gap-xs text-body-md text-body">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">A "country" cookie</strong> (up to 1 year) remembers
          which country's version of the calculator you've chosen, so you're not
          asked or redirected again.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Local storage entries</strong> save your last
          calculator and comparison inputs (fuel type, price, mileage, distance) per
          country, and your light/dark theme choice, so the site remembers your setup
          on your next visit. These stay on your device and are never transmitted to
          our servers as a stored record.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-ink">Page URLs</strong> — the calculator mirrors your
          inputs into the page's URL (e.g. <code class="text-code">?fuel=petrol&price=105</code>)
          so you can copy and share a link that reproduces your exact setup. Because
          this is part of the URL, it's visible to anyone you share the link with and
          appears in standard web server access logs the same as any URL, including
          Cloudflare's (our hosting provider — see below).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        You can clear all of this at any time through your browser's cookie and site
        data settings — the site works fine afterward, it just stops remembering your
        last inputs and preferences.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Country detection (IP address)</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        On your first visit to the homepage, if you haven't already picked a country
        (no cookie set yet) and you're not a recognised search-engine crawler, our
        server sends your IP address to <strong class="text-ink">ip-api.com</strong>,
        a third-party geolocation service, to determine your approximate country and
        offer to show you that country's version of the calculator. We don't store
        this IP address ourselves beyond that one lookup, and it's never linked to
        any other data we hold about you (we don't hold any). ip-api.com's own
        handling of that request is governed by their policies at
        <a href="https://ip-api.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">ip-api.com</a>.
        You can always override the detected country yourself using the switcher in
        the site's navigation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Location and the fuel-station finder</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        The "Find fuel stations near you" feature only requests your device's precise
        location if you click "Show nearby stations" and your browser prompts you to
        allow it — it's never requested automatically. If you allow it, your
        coordinates are used directly by your browser to load a Google Maps embed
        centred on your location; we don't route this through, or store it on, our
        own servers. If you decline or your browser doesn't support geolocation, the
        map falls back to a general view of your selected city or country instead.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        The Google Maps embed and the "Open in Google Maps" link are Google services,
        governed by
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
        The map only loads once you actively click to show it — it's not embedded on
        page load.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Hosting and infrastructure</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        This site runs on Cloudflare's network (Cloudflare Workers, Pages, and KV
        storage for cached fuel-price data). Cloudflare processes standard request
        data — IP address, user agent, request URL — to serve the site and for its
        own security/performance logging, governed by
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.
        We don't operate a separate analytics or tracking service on top of this.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Advertising</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        Fuel Calculate does not currently display third-party advertising. If we
        introduce advertising in future (for example, through Google AdSense), that
        network and its partners may use cookies to serve ads based on your visits to
        this and other sites. You'll be able to opt out of personalised advertising
        at any time via
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">Google's Ads Settings</a>
        or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">aboutads.info</a>,
        and we'll update this policy and, where required (for example for visitors in
        the UK or EU), request your consent before any such ads are shown.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        This site isn't directed at children and we don't knowingly collect personal
        data from anyone under 13 (or the relevant minimum age in your country).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        Because we don't hold a database of personal information about you, most
        privacy requests are handled directly through your own browser — clearing
        cookies and local storage removes everything the site has stored about your
        visit. If you're in the UK or EU, you have rights under GDPR/UK GDPR
        (including access, correction, deletion, and objection); if you're a
        California resident, you have rights under the CCPA/CPRA (including the right
        to know and delete, and to opt out of any future sale or sharing of personal
        information — which we do not do). To ask a question about any of this,
        <a href="/contact" class="text-link underline">contact us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        We'll update this page if what the site collects or how it's used changes —
        for example, if advertising is introduced — and update the "last updated"
        date above when we do.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-sm text-body-md text-body">
        Questions about this policy or your data? Email
        <a href="mailto:beststoredeal101@gmail.com" class="text-link underline">beststoredeal101@gmail.com</a>
        or visit the <a href="/contact" class="text-link underline">Contact us</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
